After thousands of dead wizards, I'm playing tourists now. They're good
fun; it's nice to experiment with different weapons and armour, not
worry about food in the early game, and also to try for the protection
racket. I also play them vegan, which is surprisingly easy (although
the lack of intrinsics later might hurt). Only barely getting them to
minetown at the moment, but still good fun.

Anyway, after a very dull first level, Gurnpepper the tourist found a
jewelry store on Dlevel2. He had entered the dungeon with a tripe
ration, so he decided to stand in the shop doorway and use the old
four-paw-discount. All was going to plan. The eventually dog brought an
obsidian ring, and Gurnpepper rewarded him appropriately. Since the
ring was clearly not cursed, Gurnpepper decided to try it on and see if
it auto-IDed. Nothing. Wait a few turns, still nothing, so he removes
the ring. Dog brings over a twisted ring: Try it on, nothing, take it
off. Now the dog fetches another ring. Try it on: The shopkeeper hits!
The shopkeeper hits! DYWYPI?

That'll be the conflict, then.



